section__
  @title "T196 - ACT3 - Pyke Hostage Exchange at the broken tower"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/03-act3-stormlands/frame-196.jpg"

  "Pyke Hostage Exchange at the broken tower throws you into a theater of banners, rain, and disputed succession. Thunder rolls over flooded fields, and campfires hiss out faster than squires can relight them. Banner heirs press for visible favoritism, and veteran sergeants ask whether your promises survive the next weather turn. The realm survived Act Two by triage; in this theater, triage now looks like favoritism unless you enforce terms in public.

This module is claim enforcement under siege pressure: lawful sequencing earns legitimacy but can lose castles to weather windows, while covert pressure speeds compliance and poisons the alliance you need for the final wars. If you prioritize one banner publicly, you gain a reliable spearpoint and risk a broader defection; if you broker secret concessions, you keep numbers now and invite revenge once the storm passes.

